<Doc title="Privacy · Tracend" description="What Tracend collects in the app and on this website, how AI features use it with your consent, who processes it, and how to export or delete it.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="doc-date">Last updated 2 November 2026</p>
  <p class="doc-lede">The short version: we use your data to coach you and to run the beta, nothing else. No AI feature receives your data until you agree, and the app names the company it uses before you do. We never sell your data or use it for ads. You can export everything or delete your account from the app at any time.</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>Tracend is a personal trainer app for iPhone, best with Apple Watch, in a private, invite-only beta. This page covers the app, this website and the beta waitlist. Tracend decides how and why your data is used, which makes us its controller.</p>
  <p>For anything about your data, including a complaint, write to our grievance contact at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We reply within a few days and settle a complaint within one month.</p>

  <h2>What we collect in the app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your email address and a password you choose. We don&rsquo;t store the password in readable form, and we don&rsquo;t ask for your name.</li>
    <li><strong>Your profile and goal:</strong> what you tell us when you set up, such as your goal, age, sex, height, weight, training days, equipment, current lifts, limits, movements to avoid and diet notes.</li>
    <li><strong>Your training:</strong> the plans you approve, and your workouts with sets, reps, loads and effort.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple Health data you allow:</strong> steps, active energy, sleep, workouts, weight, resting heart rate, heart rate during your workouts, heart rate while you sleep, heart rate variability (HRV) and breathing rate. Sleeping heart rate is worked out on your phone, and only one summary per night leaves it. You choose each type in iOS, and the app works without it.</li>
    <li><strong>Food:</strong> the meals you log, and meal photos if you take them.</li>
    <li><strong>Progress:</strong> weight, body measurements, morning check-ins, pain you report and progress photos.</li>
    <li><strong>Coach:</strong> the messages you send the Coach and its replies.</li>
    <li><strong>Your choices:</strong> each consent you give or withdraw, when, and which notice you saw.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash and performance reports:</strong> technical details when the app or our servers hit an error or run slowly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect on this website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your email address</strong>, if you join the waitlist, and whether you have confirmed it, unsubscribed or been invited.</li>
    <li><strong>Your consent:</strong> when you gave it and which wording you saw.</li>
    <li><strong>Referrals:</strong> your invite code, and who invited you if you came from a friend&rsquo;s link.</li>
    <li><strong>Where you came from:</strong> campaign tags in the link you used (for example <code>utm_source</code>) and your browser&rsquo;s time zone. We don&rsquo;t record your location.</li>
    <li><strong>A scrambled form of your IP address</strong> (a salted hash), kept for 24 hours to stop repeated sign-ups from one network. We never store the address itself.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The site sets no cookies of its own and runs no advertising or analytics trackers.</p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>To coach you:</strong> build your plan, read your recovery each morning, track your progress and answer your questions.</li>
    <li><strong>To keep the app working and safe:</strong> fix errors and stop abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>To run the waitlist:</strong> confirm your email, invite people in order and send you news about the beta.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We rely on your consent, which you can withdraw at any time. We never sell your data, share it for advertising, or use Apple Health data for marketing.</p>

  <h2>Your health data, only with your explicit consent</h2>
  <p>Your Apple Health data, check-ins, pain reports, body measurements and photos are health data. When you set up the app, you agree to us using them with a tick box of its own, separate from accepting the terms, and the app records which version of this notice you agreed to. We use them only to coach you and to keep the app working, as this page describes.</p>
  <p>You can withdraw this consent by deleting your account, or by emailing us. Tracend can&rsquo;t coach you without it, so withdrawing ends your use of the app.</p>

  <h2>AI features, only with your consent</h2>
  <p>Some features use an AI model run by another company. Before a feature sends anything, the app shows a notice that says what it sends, which company receives it and where that company processes it, and asks you to agree. If you say no, nothing is sent.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Coach chat and the daily decision</strong> send your plan and workouts, check-ins, Apple Health summaries, meals and nutrition targets, body measurements, goals and preferences, and the messages you send the Coach.</li>
    <li><strong>Your starting plan</strong> sends your setup answers and, if you connected Apple Health, summaries of your recent weeks and your usual months.</li>
    <li><strong>Meal photo estimates</strong> send a resized copy of the one photo you choose to analyze, and nothing else.</li>
    <li><strong>The physique check:</strong> if you use it, the progress photos you choose are sent, after you agree to its notice, to the company that notice names, with your sex, height, latest weight, body measurements and goal. Photo details such as location are removed first.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Progress photos go to AI only through the physique check, and only after you agree. No AI feature receives your name or email address.</p>
  <p>What an AI returns is a suggestion or an estimate. Your plan only changes when you approve it, a meal only counts once you confirm it, and a physique suggestion only becomes your focus if you choose it.</p>
  <p>We don&rsquo;t sell your data or share it for model training. Each AI company&rsquo;s own terms decide whether it keeps a request and for how long; the feature&rsquo;s notice tells you before you agree.</p>

  <h2>Who processes your data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> (Singapore) hosts the app&rsquo;s accounts, database, photos and server code, and stores the waitlist.</li>
    <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> (United States) runs the AI models behind Coach chat and the daily decision. Other features, and any feature we move, can use Anthropic, <strong>Groq</strong> (United States) or <strong>DeepSeek</strong> (China). Each feature uses one company at a time, named in that feature&rsquo;s notice, and only after you agree to it. Moving a feature to another company always shows you a new notice and asks you again first, and a new company is added here before it receives anything.</li>
    <li><strong>Sentry</strong> (United States) receives crash, error and performance reports. A report can carry your account ID and device and app details, never your name or email. Health values, meal content, photo links and prompts are stripped before it is sent.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong> runs our deployments and stores encrypted database backups (the newest 30).</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website, which means it receives standard request data such as your IP address and browser, and runs Turnstile, the bot check on the join form, which looks at your browser and IP address to tell people from bots.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> sends our waitlist emails, through Gmail.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>Your account and everything you log are stored by Supabase on servers in Singapore, in private storage other accounts can&rsquo;t reach. Progress photos open through links that expire after one minute. Data an AI feature sends is processed in the country listed above for that company, and the feature&rsquo;s notice says so too. Where your data leaves your country, we rely on each provider&rsquo;s data processing terms, including the EU Standard Contractual Clauses where a provider offers them.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your account and logs:</strong> until you delete them or your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Meal photos:</strong> deleted about 7 days after you take them, or sooner if you discard the meal. The foods you confirm stay in your log.</li>
    <li><strong>Progress photos:</strong> until you delete the photo set or your account. Physique check results go with their photo set.</li>
    <li><strong>Coach conversations:</strong> until you delete the conversation or your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Exports:</strong> deleted after three downloads or seven days, whichever comes first.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> up to 30 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Backups:</strong> we keep the newest 30 encrypted database backups. After you delete your account, your data leaves them as newer backups replace older ones.</li>
    <li><strong>Deleted accounts:</strong> we keep a receipt with no content for 180 days. Your email comes off the invite list and the waitlist when you delete your account; to come back, join the waitlist again.</li>
    <li><strong>AI companies:</strong> each company&rsquo;s own terms decide whether it keeps a request and for how long. The feature&rsquo;s notice tells you before you agree.</li>
    <li><strong>The waitlist:</strong> while the waitlist and beta run. If you never confirm your email, we delete your signup 30 days after our last email. If you unsubscribe, we keep your signup marked unsubscribed so we never email you by mistake. Deleting your app account deletes your waitlist signup too. Ask us and we delete it completely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your controls</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Export:</strong> download everything you have logged, photos included, from the app. The file is locked with a password only you know.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete:</strong> delete your account from the app. Your profile, logs, photos, Coach conversations, exports, waitlist signup and place on the invite list are deleted with it. We keep only the receipt, described above.</li>
    <li><strong>Turn AI off:</strong> turn off AI coaching in Account, or meal photo analysis in Log a meal. Sending stops at once. Your plan, logging, Apple Health sync and progress keep working without AI.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple Health:</strong> change what Tracend can read in the iOS Health settings at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent history:</strong> see each choice you made, and when, in Account.</li>
    <li><strong>Email us</strong> to see, correct or delete your data, or to leave the waitlist. Every waitlist email has a one-tap unsubscribe link. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>Tracend is for adults. Don&rsquo;t join or use the app if you are under 18.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about your data or this policy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we update this page and the date at the top, and the app asks you to agree again before you carry on. If a change affects how we use your email, we tell you by email first. If an AI feature changes what it sends or which company receives it, the app shows a new notice and asks for your consent again before sending anything.</p>
</Doc>
